Z||000031||AusFiero||08-17-2001||04:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Max The Chainsaw:<BR><B>To me, the notchback style just says "Fiero" while the fastback is too easily confused with so many other cars out there.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep easliy confused with Ferarri I found locally. I looked at an 85 GT before getting my 86 1/2 one. 2 reasons. The notchback rear does not match the GT nose, square at one end and sloped at the other. The fastbacks look right from a design point of view. Thats the reason I put more shape in my notchback designs I did. The back is wrong from a styling point of view.  Main reason. The 4 speed gearbox annoyed the hell out of me at highway speeds. Just felt like it needed that other gear as it revved its head off. <BR>Yep, there are some nice 85 GT's out there and everyone has their own tastes. Thats just my opinions. Stll would love an Indy though.<BR>Aus puts his flame retardent suit on now too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
